<div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 mb-3">Rate Limits & Traffic Policing</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
        API-key limits are checked before AI provider work. The key record can define requests per minute (RPM) and requests per day (RPD); configured limits are enforced across the API-key guarded endpoints.
    </p>

    <div class="border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/50 rounded-xl p-4 mb-8 flex gap-3 items-start">
        <i class="fas fa-tachometer-alt text-amber-600 mt-0.5"></i>
        <p class="text-amber-900 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Per-key settings:</strong> Configure RPM and RPD from the API Keys page. Changing a key's limits applies to subsequent requests. Empty limits mean no per-key cap for that window.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Standard Operational Limit Bounds</h2>
    <div class="overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm mb-8">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-200 text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-50">
                <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-slate-700">Metric Target Class</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-slate-700">Default Sandbox Threshold</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-slate-700">Tracking Logic Interval</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 text-slate-600 bg-white">
                <tr>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Requests per Minute (RPM)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-slate-800">60 reqs/min</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3">Counter resets 60 seconds after the bucket reset time.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Requests per Day (RPD)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-slate-800">1,000 reqs/day</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3">Counter resets 24 hours after the bucket reset time; this is not a midnight UTC reset.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900">Monthly Token Volume Limit</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600">Not enforced</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3">A monthly token value can be stored on a key, but it is not currently checked by request handling.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-3">Limit Exceeded</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">When a configured RPM or RPD limit is reached, the gateway responds with HTTP <code>429</code>. The response does not currently include rate-limit headers.</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">{
  "statusCode": 429,
    "message": "API key requests-per-minute limit exceeded",
    "error": "Too Many Requests"
}</code></pre>

    <div class="border-l-4 p-4 mt-6 rounded-r-xl bg-emerald-50/60 border-emerald-500 flex gap-3 items-start">
        <i class="fas fa-lightbulb text-emerald-600 mt-0.5"></i>
        <p class="text-emerald-950 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <strong>Client guidance:</strong> Wait for the documented window to reset before retrying. Use bounded exponential backoff for transient 429 responses.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>